        "id": 1119068
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-02-13T16:11:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should better use:\n\n   u64 sched_clock_cpu(smp_processor_id())\n\ninstead of ktime_t and ktime_get(), for all the enqueue/dequeue paths:\n\n   schedtune_{en,de}queue_task()\n      schedtune_tasks_update()\n\nwhich are also under rq lock.\n\nPotentially we can also use the rq-\u003eclock directly, provided we do not do updates at CGroups attach/detach time, which I think we can avoid completely... (look at my following comment)",
      "revId": "7a2ae52abcc8cf60b8c1b0413eace0411dd7656d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
