      "writtenOn": "2018-02-13T16:11:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe this one also can be skipped... since we do not actually trigger a schedutil update when we move tasks among cgroups, we can probably just wait for the task to be dequeue/enqueued one time before actually holding its boost in the new CPU, which will avoid also the next chunk (thus simplifying the login we are adding).\n\nAnother reason to remove it is that we do not update the timeout for the SRC cpu... thus, for consistency probably better to not poke with the destination one.",
